From e2573888f2bb9dd325cc8f20890d72b281e39bf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:00:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix render-blocking deps, cursor/SAPI defaults, screenshot
 grounding, scene pacing, tests

- requirements.txt: add opencv-python + numpy (video_service.py imports
  cv2/numpy but neither was declared; a clean install could not render
  video at all). Drop unused pyttsx3.
- .env.example: OLLAMA_VISION_ENABLED=true and TTS_PROVIDER=sapi by
  default, matching the actual product requirement (cursor grounding
  + Windows SAPI narration). Removed documentation for azure/auto/
  local_hinglish TTS providers since tts_service._generate_one() does
  not implement them in this branch -- setting them previously fell
  back to Kokoro silently.
- tts_service.py: hardcoded fallback default changed from kokoro to
  sapi so behavior is correct even with no .env file present.
- ai_service.py: _select_screenshot_and_visual() replaces the old
  behavior of always reusing the first screenshot found on a step's
  page. For actions, it now grounds against every same-page
  screenshot candidate and keeps whichever one Qwen actually finds
  the control in. Also fixes compound-action splitting leaving later
  pieces lowercase mid-sentence in captions.
- video_service.py: added MIN_SCENE_SECONDS floor + SCENE_PADDING_SECONDS
  so short narration clips (e.g. "Click Save.") can't produce a scene
  too short to show the cursor animation or let a viewer read the
  caption.
- tests/test_core.py: rewritten against the functions that actually
  exist today (previous suite failed at import/collection -- it
  referenced three functions removed in an earlier refactor). Added
  coverage for the screenshot-grounding fix and the duration floor.
